# ── Gradle / JVM ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
vectorbea-proxy/build/
vectorbea-proxy/.gradle/
.gradle/
*.class
*.war
*.ear
# Exclude compiled JARs but keep Gradle wrapper JARs (required for CI)
#
# The exception below used to name `vectorbea-proxy/`, a directory that no longer
# exists. So the rule read as "exclude every jar", and all three wrapper jars were
# silently untracked — present on every developer's disk, absent from every clone.
#
# That is invisible until something runs `./gradlew` on a fresh checkout, and then it
# fails with `Unable to access jarfile .../gradle-wrapper.jar`. It bit a Railway build
# (which had auto-detected Gradle) and it applies equally to the `bash ./gradlew build`
# steps in CI. The service Dockerfiles were unaffected only because they invoke the
# `gradle` binary directly rather than the wrapper.
*.jar
!**/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

